.TH turrule n 0.2 tclutils
.SH tclutils::turrule
.PP
Expand iCalendar \fBRRULE\fR recurrence rules into concrete occurrences.
.PP
Supported subset of RFC 5545: \fBFREQ\fR DAILY/WEEKLY/MONTHLY/YEARLY, \fBINTERVAL\fR, \fBCOUNT\fR, \fBUNTIL\fR, \fBBYMONTH\fR, \fBBYDAY\fR and \fBBYMONTHDAY\fR, \fBWKST=MO\fR. Date math is done in UTC for calendar stability.
.TS
l l.
Part	Meaning
\fBBYDAY\fR	weekday list (\fBMO,WE\fR); with MONTHLY/YEARLY also ordinals (\fB1MO\fR, \fB4TH\fR, \fB\-1FR\fR)
\fBBYMONTHDAY\fR	day list, negatives count from the month end; not with WEEKLY
\fBBYMONTH\fR	month list 1–12; YEARLY expands to these months, other frequencies are limited to them
.TE
.PP
YEARLY expands like this: with \fBBYMONTH\fR each listed month (a \fBBYDAY\fR ordinal counts within the month: \fBBYMONTH=11;BYDAY=4TH\fR is the fourth Thursday of November); without \fBBYMONTH\fR a \fBBYMONTHDAY\fR applies to every month, and a \fBBYDAY\fR ordinal counts within the year (\fBBYDAY=20MO\fR); without any of them the DTSTART month and day. When \fBBYDAY\fR and \fBBYMONTHDAY\fR are both given, only days matching both remain (\fBFREQ=MONTHLY;BYDAY=FR;BYMONTHDAY=13\fR).
.PP
\fBUNTIL\fR as a date (\fBUNTIL=20250120\fR) includes that whole day; with a time it is exact.
.PP
Any other rule part — \fBBYSETPOS\fR, \fBBYWEEKNO\fR, \fBBYYEARDAY\fR, \fBBYHOUR\fR, \fBBYMINUTE\fR, \fBBYSECOND\fR, \fBWKST\fR other than \fBMO\fR, an unknown name — raises \fB{TCLUTILS TURRULE UNSUPPORTED}\fR instead of being ignored.
.SS API
.CS
::tclutils::turrule::parse "FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=TU,TH;COUNT=4"   ;# -> dict

::tclutils::turrule::occurrences -dtstart 2025-10-01 \
    -rule "FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=TU,TH;COUNT=4" -from 2025-01-01 -to 2025-12-31
#  -> 2025-10-02 2025-10-07 2025-10-09 2025-10-14
.CE
.PP
Commands:
.IP \(bu
\fBparse rrule\fR → dict of upper\-case parts.
.IP \(bu
\fBoccurrences \-dtstart ISO \-rule RRULE ?\-from ISO? ?\-to ISO? ?\-count N?\fR → occurrence list. \fBCOUNT\fR is counted from DTSTART; \fB\-from/\-to\fR only window the output. The result must be bounded by \fB\-to\fR, \fB\-count\fR, \fBCOUNT\fR or \fBUNTIL\fR (else \fB{TCLUTILS TURRULE UNBOUNDED}\fR). Date\-only DTSTART yields dates; a datetime DTSTART preserves the time of day.
.IP \(bu
\fBeventsInRange ics fromIso toIso\fR → list of \fB{uid summary start}\fR for every VEVENT occurrence in range (uses \fBtclutils::tuical\fR to parse). An RRULE with an unsupported part raises the error of \fBoccurrences\fR.
.SS Errors
.PP
\fB{TCLUTILS TURRULE <REASON>}\fR:
.TS
l l.
Reason	When
\fBFREQ\fR	no \fBFREQ\fR, or an unsupported one
\fBUNBOUNDED\fR	no \fB\-to\fR, \fB\-count\fR, \fBCOUNT\fR or \fBUNTIL\fR
\fBDATE\fR	a date that cannot be read
\fBUNSUPPORTED\fR	a rule part outside the subset above
\fBBYDAY\fR	unknown weekday code, ordinal 0 or above 53, ordinal with DAILY/WEEKLY
\fBVALUE\fR	\fBBYMONTH\fR outside 1–12, \fBBYMONTHDAY\fR outside ±1–31 or not an integer
.TE
